# CREDITS — One Rectangle

A 40-second film in the Ukiyo-e style, made entirely in code.
The shore, the raker and the rectangle are invented. No real place, person or brand is portrayed.

## Voice
Speech synthesis: Kokoro (kokoro-onnx), voice `af_heart`, English, offline.
Model and engine: https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx
(Apache-2.0 for kokoro-onnx; the weights follow that project's terms).

## Music
Original score for this film (`music/score.py`). No existing melody.
Shamisen and koto are physically modelled (`core/audio/pluck.py`, Karplus–Strong).
Shakuhachi, wind, rake, tide, baren, gull, clappers and the seal are synthesised in `music/score.py` and `mix.py`.
No sample library is used.

## Typefaces
Cormorant Garamond, roman and italic — SIL Open Font License 1.1.
Copyright 2015 The Cormorant Project Authors (github.com/CatharsisFonts/Cormorant).
Copies of the OFL files used by the Impasto demo, in `fonts/`.

## Picture
Every frame is drawn by this film's own print code (`print.js`, `scene.js`, `main.js`).
No photographs, no scans, no third-party images.
